<header>
<h1>Thomas Nush Holykeyz Que Jr.</h1>
<p>Mathematics Educator | Liberia</p>
</header>

<h2>About Me</h2>
<p>
Thomas Nush Holykeyz Que Jr. is a Liberian mathematics educator
and graduate of the Kakata Rural Teacher Training Institute
(KRTTI), Margibi County, where he earned a B-Certificate
in Mathematics. He is committed to education, academic
development, and helping students achieve excellence.
</p>

<h2>Educational Background</h2>
<ul>
<li>B-Certificate in Mathematics – KRTTI, 2026.</li>
<li>C-Certificate – QTTI, 2022.</li>
<li>Diploma – Jannie Preparatory School, 2018.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Teaching Experience</h2>
<ul>
<li>Boima K. Corney Elementary & Junior High School (2019–2020).</li>
<li>New Day Elementary School, Plankside, Sinoe County (2020–2021).</li>
<li>St. Paul's Episcopal Parish High School, Greenville (2021–2024).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Professional Interest</h2>
<p>
Mathematics education, teaching, academic research,
student development, and community service.
</p>

<h2>Location</h2>
<p>Greenville, Sinoe County, Liberia.</p>

